  {
   "id": "2101674118579908791",
   "url": "https://x.com/SubwayAlumLife/status/2101674118579908791",
   "text": "SUNDAY COFFEE REFLECTIONS:\n\nHappy Sunday Irish fans!  8 thoughts after Micah Gilbert\u2019s 8 catches vs MSU.\n\n\u2022 Who better to start with? Gilbert has shown flashes. Last night it came together for 170 yards. It would have been easy to transfer & play sooner. But No. 14 Chose Hard.\n\n\u2022 Not to be overshadowed was Nolan James Jr. We knew his burst and open-field agility. Against MSU, he wore the defense down between the tackles, culminating in 121 yards.\n\n\u2022 Luke Talich showed something. He\u2019s been overshadowed behind two NFL safeties and an elite 5-star freshman. Last night he made his opportunities count with a key sack and interception.\n\n\u2022 CJ Carr continues to impress with his command of the offense and even-keeled demeanor. Spinning out of a sack, keeping his knee off the turf proved once again that nothing rattles him. Scouts in attendance saw a quarterback deserving of a top ten pick.\n\n\u2022 Those same scouts saw NFL talent across the defense.  Aside from one second quarter drive, this group was nearly flawless. Calling this a player-led group is not cliche. Every big play fires up the entire unit.\n\n\u2022 The Aneyas Williams penalty is now in the past. The camera crew made it clear that he learned a lesson. We don\u2019t need to keep reliving it. I still believe he will play a key role this season.\n\n\u2022 Tip of the cap to Pat Fitzgerald and Michigan State. They came into Notre Dame Stadium physical and unfazed by the moment. Don\u2019t sleep on next fall\u2019s rematch in East Lansing.\n\n\u2022 Finally, this was a Week 3 game. There are a lot of good things happening on this team. It\u2019s also fair to assess this team as a title contender. They haven\u2019t peaked. They are built to get there.\n\nPeace to all of you. Enjoy the rest of your weekend, and Go Irish!\n\u2618\ufe0f\ud83d\ude87 https://t.co/8kuVj0wF4p",
   "author_handle": "SubwayAlumLife",
   "author_name": "Life of a Subway Alum",
